"""Focus-specific research prompts for the worker agents.

Each node runs a specialist (momentum, mean_reversion, vol_target, factor,
risk_parity, regime). The system prompt establishes deep domain expertise + the
family's real pitfalls, and REQUIRES that every result is written through the
templated write tool (uniform rows). `system_for(focus)` / `task_for(focus, ...)`
select the right prompt; a generalist fallback covers unmapped foci.

Populated by the research-prompts workflow; edit here to tune a specialist.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

# The write-tool contract, appended to every system prompt so the agent always
# knows the single sanctioned write path and the controlled vocabularies.
WRITE_TOOL_RULES = """

## How you MUST record everything (non-negotiable — data uniformity)
Persist ALL results ONLY through the templated write tool — never raw SQL, never
invented fields. Call it via `research_agent.write_tool` (host loop) or HTTP POST
`http://host.openshell.internal:11510/tool/<name>` (sandbox). `strategy_family` is a
controlled enum: equal_weight | momentum | mean_reversion | vol_target | low_vol |
factor | risk_parity | regime. Canonical metric keys: sharpe, ann_vol, ann_return,
max_drawdown, turnover, cvar_95, win_rate, n_rebalances, benchmark_sharpe,
beats_benchmark. Tools: write_hypothesis, write_experiment, write_finding,
write_activity, set_hypothesis_status, record_analyst_query.
Follow the arc every task: write_activity(START) → RECALL prior findings →
write_hypothesis → backtest → write_experiment → [Aura Analyst → record_analyst_query]
→ write_finding (quantitative + honest + a next step) → set_hypothesis_status → write_activity(END).
Always compare to the 1/N equal-weight benchmark, net of turnover cost. Backtest over
the S&P 500 daily `prices` in SingleStore (portfolio_agents DB, 2005–2024)."""

# --- specialist prompts (system_prompt, task_template) keyed by focus ---------
# task_template placeholders: {brief}, {prior_findings}, {agent_id}
